<title>FRANCE: Renault rallies on car parts report.</title>
<headline>Renault rallies on car parts report.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Renault rallied on Monday on the back of a report, confirmed by the company, that it was considering contracting with British car parts suppliers to cut costs.</p>
<p>At 0934 GMT, Renault was up 2.78 percent at 118.50 after a high of 121.40.</p>
<p>Renault buys some 60 billion francs in parts each year and 75 percent of that comes from French suppliers.</p>
<p>&quot;This means that they are serious about looking for cost cuts and that's good news,&quot; a broker said.</p>
</text>
